WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.000
-Lucy, we love you.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.701
Thanks for coming
back to the show.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.334
-It's so great
to see you guys again.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.968
-Um, do you --
I was going to ask you,

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:08.167
and this is a real question.
-Okay.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.501
-Because I follow you
on socials,

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:10.767
and Instagram and stuff.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.100
Do you --
you've been all over the world.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.934
Do you know where
you are right now?

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.467
-I just got in last night,
so, no, I don't know.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:19.467
I don't know what time it is --
-Weren't you just in Italy?

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:20.634
-This is perfect.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:21.868
-Weren't you just in Italy,
I just saw --

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.868
-Yeah, I was in --
we were in Rome.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.267
We went to London.
I was in Toronto --

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.968
-Wow.
-L.A.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.434
-Everything.
And now you're going right back

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.534
to L.A.
-And then I go back to L.A.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:31.868
for the premiere,
which will be exciting.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.100
-Thank you for being here
on our show.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.634
-No, I'm so happy it worked out.
-We appreciate it.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.400
How is everything --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.934
We love you.

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.334
I want to talk about the movie,
but how's Rockwell?

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:41.400
How's the baby?
How's the baby?

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.901
-Oh, he's 7.
He's 7.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.000
-No, isn't that weird.
-Can you believe it?

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.300
He's a little man.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.501
-I remember when, I mean,
he was just strapped to you.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.033
-Yeah, he was, like,
a meat puff.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.734
-Yeah, he's so cute.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.901
You were saying that he got to
meet Helen Mirren,

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:56.334
Dame Hellen Mirren, who's in --
-No, this isn't just a meeting.

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:58.467
-Oh.
-This was like a meeting of the

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.100
minds and the heart.
-Wow.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.534
-Yeah, so, I'm in my -- in my
trailer, and she's like,

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:04.367
"Oh, your son is here.
I want to come and meet him."

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.300
-Yeah.
-So she comes and -- I mean,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.734
you don't have to do that,
by the way.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.167
-No, of course not.
She's the best.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.601
-She's the best.
-Yeah, she's cool.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:13.100
-So she comes in and sits down
in the trailer with him for

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.868
like, I don't know,
15, 20 minutes.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:17.901
Just talks to him,
spends some time with him.

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:19.968
And then she's like,
"Oh, I've got to go get ready."

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:23.000
So she leaves and then he turns
to me and he's like,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.667
"mommy, do you know who
I'm going to marry?"

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.667
And I was like,
"where is this coming from?

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.868
Does, how does he even
know what that is?"

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.400
-Yeah.
-I'm like, "no, who?"

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.834
He's like, "Helen."

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:33.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.100
And then I was like -- and I so
shocked, I was like,

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.033
"well, what if she's
already married?"

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:39.400
He was like,
"Then I'll just be her butler."

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.167
I was like "oh, that's what
a husband is."

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.601
-Come on, that's a 7-year-old --
-A butler or a husband.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.167
-Yeah, exactly.
-It was hysterical.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.334
-He's so cute.
-But that's the --

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:50.567
-The effect?
-The effect she has on people.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:51.734
-The Helen Mirren --
-She's just so present.

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.234
-Yeah, even babies want
to marry her.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.033
-Oh, my -- He was 5!

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.200
-Five when he said that?
-So it's like, pure instinct.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.434
-I love him.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:58.934
I want to talk about this,
'cause it's going around

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.667
the Internet, and I want to get
your take on it.

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:03.300
Our pal, Drew Barrymore,
who we love --

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.634
-Yes.
-said last month that

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.667
she'd be up for making another
"Charlie's Angels"

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.367
if you and Cameron --

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:10.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.601
If you and Cameron
were up for it as well.

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:13.968
-Well that's no pressure.

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:17.367
I mean, it's -- let's just say,
guys, it's been 23 years.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.634
-Has it really?
-Yes, it's been 23 --

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:20.701
it's a long time.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.234
-but still, look, 23 years --

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:23.334
I mean, you still
look like a baby.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:24.634
-No, I feel great.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.667
But I just mean, it's going to
be a different iteration

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:29.033
of a "Charlie's Angels,"
I guess.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.167
-Yeah, I don't know.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.634
-But, you know,
I love them so much.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.634
It'd be -- it would be really
fun to do anything with them.

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:35.634
But, like, I just -- it's so --

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.400
It seems like it was yesterday,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.534
and it seems like it was so
far away at the same time.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:42.300
You know, like, the wire work
and all the Kung Fu, and --

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.934
-Did you guys do Comic-Con
for that one too?

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.234
No, you didn't.
That's not Comic-Con.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:47.767
-No, we did comic-con for
"Shazam!" which was insane.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.000
I've never been in a theater
like that before.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.033
-I was gonna say, like, 'cause I
know, yeah, for "Shazam!"

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:53.334
you have to go to Comic-Con.

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:54.968
But it's like -- well, you
get to go to comic-con.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.300
-No, it's because it's
a DC movie, you know?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.767
And they really expect it.

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:00.667
And they have a special trailer
and a preview just for the fans.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:02.133
-What is it like?
-These are not fans.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.267
I mean, I'm sure you kind of
know about this, but these are,

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.100
like, superfans.
-Yes.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.334
-So, it sort of even predates
anything you could do

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.901
as a person, as an actor,
as anyone.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:14.400
Because they know everything.
-Before you were even were in

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.968
the movie, they know your
character.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.000
-No, they know the history of
all the characters,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.667
the comic books,
the movies, all of it.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.000
You know, and for me, like,
I grew up just reading

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.868
the comic books.
So, it's very different.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.801
Like, all the things that are
out now, it's just insanely,

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:29.667
you know -- I mean, you just
can't match the CGI

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.133
and all the special effects.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.801
-Well, this film, you're flying
on a dragon the whole time.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:35.801
It's amazing.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:36.801
But I mean, what --

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.234
-Yeah, the dragon
is the star, okay?

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.133
Because this -- like,
look how small I am here.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:41.767
-No, I know.

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.067
-The dragon is like
the entire --

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:44.567
-But what are you actually
riding on?

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:45.634
This is a new technology?

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:47.100
-Yeah, this is
one of the first.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.767
I was like a Guinea pig.
It was a --

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:52.367
a mechanism that was for cars.
-Yeah.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:56.067
-And I would sit on this --
they put a seat there for me.

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:59.501
-And it was a rig, and I was
kind of attached to it

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.701
with a wire, and a seat,
the whole thing.

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:03.934
-So, like a mechanical bull?
-Yeah, so --

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:05.601
It was basically riding
a bronco.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:06.901
And they had different speeds,

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:07.968
and it was connected
to a computer.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:08.968
-Just like riding --

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:11.934
[ Laughter ]
-Woo!

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.334
A cowboy hat --
-Yeah, instead of the hat,

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.400
I had a crown.
Be like, "whoo-hoo!"

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.133
But it was amazing.
-And then they add in --

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:19.200
-But it was connected to the
camera,

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.567
it was connected to their
computer,

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:23.534
so they had really specific
ideas of what they wanted,

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:26.434
and they could repeat
the exact movement every time.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.834
-It's fascinating.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.734
They did such a great job.
-I can't --

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:30.801
-I would say go see this in --

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:32.000
-And this dragon
is made out of wood.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.033
-Yeah, by the way.

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:36.200
-It doesn't even have scales.
It's wood, so it's different.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.400
-But I would say go see it in
IMAX

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.100
because it's just beautiful.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.167
-Oh, it's completely insane.
-Stunning.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.501
And how do we set up the movie,

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.267
and who you play in "Shazam"?

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:48.100
-So, the movie is,
you know, these kids

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.000
that basically get these super
powers when they say, "Shazam."

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.701
And we come in, instead of as
superheroes,

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.734
we come in as goddesses.
-Yeah.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:56.934
-So, it's Greek mythology.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:58.167
-Yeah!
-Which is really cool.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.267
So we come in, and we -- our
world is dying,

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:01.701
and we're the daughters
of Atlas.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.300
So, we have to come back and
claim what's rightfully ours.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.667
So, Rachel, Helen, and I --
Rachel, who I love so much --

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:12.033
we have decided that we are the
protagonists in our story.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:13.767
-Yeah.
-Yeah, 'cause we've come to
save our world.

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.234
-Yeah, and so you're not --
yeah, you're the protagonist.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.634
-Yeah, because everyone's like,
"You're the supervillains!"

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:18.734
We're like, "are we?"
-No.

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:19.767
In our heads --

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:20.868
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:22.300
That's not the way a villain --
-No.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.300
We're, like, saving our world.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.534
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:28.400
Here's Lucy Liu in
"Shazam!: Fury of the Gods."

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.634
Take a look at this.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:31.367
♪♪

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.167
[ Inhaling deeply ]

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:40.901
♪♪

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.834
[ Overlapping whispering ]

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.434
[ Grunts ]

00:05:45.434 --> 00:05:47.834
♪♪

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.634
[ Alarm sounding ]

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.534
[ Shouting indistinctly ]

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:57.868
♪♪

00:05:57.868 --> 00:06:04.267
♪♪

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:05.901
-No, no.

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:13.667
♪♪

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.367
-[ Grunts ]

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:17.033
♪♪

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:18.400
-Woo!

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:21.634
Lucy Liu, everybody!

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:26.901
"Shazam! Fury of the Gods" opens
in theaters and IMAX March 17th.

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:29.334
Lucy and I are doing something
fun after the break.

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:30.801
Stick around.

